Description: A design-aware workflow for nonparametric, rank-based, permutation,
    resampling and robust inference in agricultural experiments. The package
    represents the randomization structure explicitly and integrates analysis of
    completely randomized, randomized complete block, factorial, split-plot, split-split, strip-plot, multi-environment, multivariate,
    repeated-measures and incomplete repeated-measures experiments. It provides
    effect estimates, design-aware Conover comparisons, nonparametric,
    integer-support and shape-constrained regression, multiplicity-aware
    contrasts, ggplot2/Plotly
    graphics, sensitivity analyses, batch workflows and reproducible reports.
    An experimental native
    wild-bootstrap engine implements rank-based quadratic-form inference for
    incompletely observed repeated measurements following Amro, Konietschke and
    Pauly (2024) under the assumptions documented by that method.
